event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":95,"item_id":"rs_0d48484d1ffe37d2016acbc1eac8c88197b36d16af19c30e86","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing sorting logic**\n\nI need to focus on implementing a straightforward order while keeping the last signature error preserved. When comparing Unicode codepoints, I must avoid using JavaScript's lexicographic UTF-16 approach. Instead, I'll use `Array.from` for the comparator, ensuring a stable sort by default. It’s important to make an explicit comment to clarify this just in case others need to understand the purpose behind the sorting method. That way, I can keep everything organized!"}

